  "notes": [
    "MSP is a price at which designated central/state agencies (FCI, NAFED, NCCF, CCI for cotton, JCI for jute, and state agencies) procure Fair Average Quality (FAQ) produce. It is not a guaranteed market price: whether procurement happens for a given crop, district or mandi depends on procurement operations (e.g. PM-AASHA Price Support Scheme for pulses/oilseeds) and state participation.",
    "MSP is announced for 22 mandated crops (14 kharif, 6 rabi, plus copra and raw jute), with FRP for sugarcane. Toria and de-husked coconut MSPs are derived from rapeseed-mustard and copra respectively; their values are not stated in the PIB releases used here and are therefore not listed.",
    "Crops WITHOUT MSP: almost all vegetables (onion, tomato, potato, brinjal, etc.), fruits (grapes, pomegranate, banana, mango, orange/citrus etc.), most spices (turmeric, chilli etc.), flowers, milk, poultry and fisheries. For onion and other perishables, prices are market-determined; some may be covered by the Market Intervention Scheme / Price Deficiency Payment components of PM-AASHA when a state requests it, which is not an MSP.",
    "Maharashtra-relevant MSP crops: cotton, soybean, tur, moong, urad, jowar, bajra, maize, paddy, groundnut, sunflower, nigerseed (Kharif); wheat, gram, safflower (Rabi); and sugarcane FRP.",
    "Kharif 2027-28 MSPs and Copra 2027 MSPs had not been announced as of 2026-11-24; verify on pib.gov.in before showing future-season prices."
  ]
